WEBVTT

00:18.700 --> 00:23.790
I wonder when I gave up trying to get out of this picture.

00:25.540 --> 00:27.630
I can't even remember that.

00:39.470 --> 00:42.180
Can I really get out?

00:43.600 --> 00:47.020
Sorry. I will write it down.

00:47.770 --> 00:50.610
Fly high, make it

00:50.610 --> 00:53.860
Get to the new world that I seek

00:54.070 --> 01:00.370
Someday with my little wings

01:00.620 --> 01:06.750
Don't look back to the sorrow I left behind

01:07.000 --> 01:12.840
Here's my real intention I hide

01:13.300 --> 01:19.720
I wish you were here, and so just right by my side

01:19.720 --> 01:25.810
Need to be strong enough to swallow my pride

01:26.180 --> 01:31.900
I have been looking for my own style

01:31.900 --> 01:39.360
Don't give it up, here comes the life

01:42.280 --> 01:45.040
Be alive, take it

01:45.040 --> 01:48.290
Promise to find, yes I will

01:48.580 --> 01:54.750
Shining wings filled with wishes

01:55.050 --> 01:57.840
Fly high, make it

01:57.840 --> 02:01.300
Get to the new world that I seek

02:01.340 --> 02:07.810
Someday, so I believe

02:30.790 --> 02:32.000
That's me.

02:33.500 --> 02:36.000
Mother, is it okay for you to get up?

02:36.760 --> 02:38.510
I feel good today.

02:39.510 --> 02:40.550
It's beautiful, isn't it?

02:40.550 --> 02:41.510
Yeah.

02:42.180 --> 02:45.510
I had always wanted to appear in this director's movies.

02:46.470 --> 02:51.900
My dream came true, even if it was just for an instant.

02:51.900 --> 02:52.520
Dream?

02:53.020 --> 02:55.020
I hope your dream comes true too.

02:55.730 --> 02:57.690
Even if it's not a great one,

02:57.690 --> 03:00.110
as long as it's a dream that you desire from the bottom of your heart,

03:00.650 --> 03:02.450
a dream that you've had for a long time.

03:04.200 --> 03:06.240
Don't worry, Mother.

03:06.240 --> 03:08.080
Because I've already found it.

03:27.390 --> 03:28.770
Is it interesting?

03:32.270 --> 03:35.310
Sorry. Did I disturb you?

03:35.310 --> 03:37.020
No, not really.

03:37.020 --> 03:39.360
Your form was really beautiful.

03:39.360 --> 03:41.320
Can I see that?

03:41.320 --> 03:42.780
Y-Yeah.

03:44.320 --> 03:45.910
The way you shot it is bad.

03:46.780 --> 03:50.040
You only shot my face and didn't get any of my form at all.

03:50.040 --> 03:52.790
Nah, that's not what I was aiming for...

03:55.040 --> 03:58.380
Next time you shoot without my permission, I'll use my right hand.

04:00.050 --> 04:02.510
This is why the sports club...

04:04.220 --> 04:05.220
But...

04:16.150 --> 04:17.900
Which one is pointing at eleven?

04:19.400 --> 04:22.990
Kei didn't come to wake me up today, eh?

04:29.580 --> 04:32.700
Erm, can I kiss you?

04:33.120 --> 04:34.290
Renji-kun.

04:36.830 --> 04:39.340
You're Renji-kun, right?

04:39.340 --> 04:41.710
Y-Yeah, I am.

04:41.710 --> 04:43.420
You're here early today.

04:43.420 --> 04:44.970
Because I had some free time.

04:49.550 --> 04:52.180
Erm, about what happened yesterday...

04:52.180 --> 04:53.680
Yes, I remember.

04:53.850 --> 04:56.270
Ah, nah, I didn't mean to...

04:56.270 --> 04:58.440
I'm thinking of trying to write the novel.

04:59.190 --> 05:04.860
But my memory only lasts thirteen hours right now.

05:04.860 --> 05:07.200
It's impossible for me to do it by myself.

05:08.280 --> 05:11.410
It's okay. I'll help you.

05:11.410 --> 05:12.450
Okay.

05:12.450 --> 05:14.540
Let's give it a try... together.

05:14.540 --> 05:16.330
Thank you very much.

05:16.330 --> 05:20.040
Besides... you're responsible for it too.

05:20.040 --> 05:21.090
Responsible?

05:21.340 --> 05:28.840
You hugged me, confessed to me, and kissed me yesterday, right?

05:29.590 --> 05:32.510
E-Eh, erm, I didn't kiss you.

05:32.510 --> 05:34.770
You did other things, didn't you?

05:34.770 --> 05:37.190
Nah, it was inevitable in that situation...

05:37.190 --> 05:39.440
That means you took advantage of it?

05:39.440 --> 05:41.520
Nah, that's not true...

05:41.520 --> 05:43.860
Chihiro, did you write that down in your diary?

05:44.610 --> 05:46.110
I forgot about it.

05:46.780 --> 05:50.030
It's a dream I gave up on a long time ago.

05:50.820 --> 05:55.500
You reminded me of it again.

05:55.500 --> 05:56.540
Chihiro...

05:56.790 --> 05:59.540
I want to try it one more time.

06:00.540 --> 06:01.420
Okay.

06:21.900 --> 06:22.980
Miyamura-senpai!

06:23.980 --> 06:25.360
What is it?

06:25.360 --> 06:27.490
Erm... Shindou Kei-chan.

06:27.990 --> 06:29.950
I need to talk to you about something.

06:29.950 --> 06:31.780
Can you come with me?

06:32.200 --> 06:34.530
Is it going to take long?

06:34.530 --> 06:35.620
Probably.

06:35.910 --> 06:38.000
Then I don't want to hear it.

06:38.000 --> 06:39.620
I want to go home.

06:39.620 --> 06:41.120
Eh? Go home?

06:41.500 --> 06:44.790
If you have something to say, you can come along with me.

06:44.790 --> 06:48.130
If it's something you have to say even if it means you're skipping school.

06:50.260 --> 06:52.930
Well then, where should we work on it?

06:52.930 --> 06:54.300
Let's see...

06:58.270 --> 06:59.600
What's wrong?

06:59.600 --> 07:02.400
I'm confirming what time I had my meal.

07:02.730 --> 07:07.900
I had my breakfast at seven this morning. It's about time to have lunch.

07:07.900 --> 07:14.410
I see. We could eat something I make at home, but maybe we should just go somewhere to eat.

07:14.410 --> 07:15.780
You want to come with me, Chihiro?

07:16.030 --> 07:17.040
Can I?

07:17.290 --> 07:18.240
Yeah.

07:18.240 --> 07:20.250
I was a bit surprised.

07:20.250 --> 07:23.330
I'm interested in your cooking.

07:23.330 --> 07:26.210
Eh? Wh-Why am I cooking?

07:26.210 --> 07:30.050
Didn't you say "something I make at home" just now?

07:30.050 --> 07:30.880
Did I?

07:30.880 --> 07:31.800
You did.

07:31.800 --> 07:35.550
Chihiro, you actually have a good memory, don't you?

07:35.800 --> 07:38.350
If it's within thirteen hours.

07:38.350 --> 07:41.520
Oh my, oh my, oh my. Welcome.

07:41.520 --> 07:44.310
Nice to meet you. I'm Shindou Chihiro.

07:44.310 --> 07:47.940
How polite of you. I'm Asou Sumire.

07:48.190 --> 07:50.820
Are you Renji-kun's... elder sister?

07:51.070 --> 07:51.820
I'm his wife.

07:53.360 --> 07:55.410
Nah, I'm really sorry.

07:55.410 --> 07:59.490
Even though I don't really want to believe it either, she's my mother.

07:59.490 --> 08:01.580
Eh, your mother?

08:01.580 --> 08:02.580
Yes.

08:06.670 --> 08:08.710
This is my neighbor, Kuze-san.

08:08.710 --> 08:12.130
Hi. I'm a good young man with a sparkling smile.

08:12.130 --> 08:12.920
Good afternoon.

08:13.260 --> 08:14.180
Good afternoon.

08:18.510 --> 08:19.810
Is that so?

08:19.810 --> 08:23.810
So, what's your relationship with Renji?

08:24.310 --> 08:28.650
If you're asking about our relationship, I think we're just friends.

08:28.650 --> 08:31.820
Friendship doesn't exist between men and women.

08:31.820 --> 08:34.200
Hmm, is that really the case?

08:34.200 --> 08:37.320
Even though it's mostly the guy who ends up with his love unrequited.

08:37.320 --> 08:41.490
Erm, I don't think Renji-kun is like that.

08:41.490 --> 08:43.080
He's just kind.

08:43.080 --> 08:43.830
Oh my.

08:43.830 --> 08:45.250
My, my.

08:45.250 --> 08:48.080
Exactly which part of Renji do you think is good?

08:48.080 --> 08:51.340
That child looks silly even from a parent's point of view.

08:51.340 --> 08:52.960
Eh? That's not true...

08:52.960 --> 08:56.550
Or does he bring out your maternal instinct?

08:56.550 --> 08:58.390
I wonder.

08:58.390 --> 09:04.310
But I'm glad because I was worried about not hearing anything of his love life until now.

09:04.310 --> 09:06.560
I find it amusing to watch.

09:06.940 --> 09:10.860
So, which part of Renji did you fall in love with?

09:11.360 --> 09:14.030
Enough is enough. You're bothering Chihiro.

09:14.320 --> 09:17.700
My, that's not true. Right, Chihiro-chan?

09:17.700 --> 09:19.410
Yes. I'm happy.

09:19.410 --> 09:20.280
See?

09:24.660 --> 09:26.660
You came along with me after all.

09:26.660 --> 09:28.620
Because I'm the one who talked to you.

09:28.880 --> 09:30.170
You seem serious.

09:30.170 --> 09:32.630
Are you aiming to take the perfect attendance award?

09:32.630 --> 09:34.630
That doesn't matter.

09:34.920 --> 09:37.930
Then what does matter?

09:37.930 --> 09:39.430
Th-That's...

09:40.850 --> 09:42.930
This is an important time for Hirono-senpai.

09:42.930 --> 09:44.430
This is an important time for Hirono-senpai.

09:44.680 --> 09:48.060
His academic results are at a critical point and full of failing marks.

09:48.060 --> 09:51.810
His attendance record is poor too, and there's even the possibility that he'll have to repeat.

09:51.810 --> 09:54.610
But, even now, he can still save the situation.

09:54.610 --> 09:57.950
If he studies and comes to classes regularly, he can become a third-year student.

09:57.950 --> 09:58.950
If he studies and comes to classes regularly, he can become a third-year student.

09:58.950 --> 10:02.700
So please don't lure Hirono-senpai into skipping school.

10:03.910 --> 10:05.450
That's a lose-lose situation.

10:06.750 --> 10:10.420
You didn't need to throw away your perfect attendance award to talk about this.

10:10.420 --> 10:14.550
I thought I'd hear something more interesting.

10:14.550 --> 10:19.220
This isn't an issue of interesting or boring!

10:19.220 --> 10:22.800
This is about Onii-ch— Hirono-senpai's future.

10:23.300 --> 10:27.600
But shouldn't Hirono-kun think about that himself?

10:30.350 --> 10:35.230
Only Hirono-kun can decide what he's going to do.

10:35.230 --> 10:37.610
It's useless for outsiders to worry for him.

10:37.900 --> 10:40.030
Outsiders... No way...

10:40.360 --> 10:43.030
Or can you handle the responsibility?

10:43.780 --> 10:47.790
Will his future be assured as long as he goes to school?

10:48.080 --> 10:48.960
That's...

10:48.960 --> 10:52.920
If Hirono-kun refrains from doing what he wants and devotes himself to studying,

10:52.920 --> 10:56.340
can he become a successful manga artist?

10:57.380 --> 10:59.470
Hirono-kun is mature,

10:59.470 --> 11:05.220
so wouldn't he have thought about skipping school, drawing manga, studying, and all that?

11:05.220 --> 11:05.890
Am I wrong?

11:05.890 --> 11:11.100
But Onii-chan is still a student. Right now he should study...

11:11.100 --> 11:15.730
Is the world of manga artists so easy that you can come and go whenever you want?

11:16.440 --> 11:19.900
He's doing his best to draw, while enduring the pain in his hand.

11:19.900 --> 11:24.030
If that comes to nothing, can you handle the responsibility?

11:25.490 --> 11:27.330
And, Kei-chan.

11:27.740 --> 11:30.580
You're showing your honesty in the wrong place.

11:31.620 --> 11:36.460
If you remain unaware of it, you might end up hating yourself one day.

11:37.920 --> 11:41.420
If you go back now, you might still be in time for the sixth period.

11:49.600 --> 11:51.020
Thank you for the meal.

11:51.310 --> 11:55.230
I didn't think you'd be good at cooking.

11:55.230 --> 11:57.520
That's my only redeeming quality.

11:58.440 --> 12:02.530
Ah, are you even writing down what you ate?

12:02.530 --> 12:06.410
Yes, since there's a possibility for the nutrition to be biased.

12:06.410 --> 12:09.950
Today's lunch was a rare ten points.

12:07.950 --> 12:09.950
Szechuan Bean Curd

12:07.950 --> 12:09.950
Bacon and Eggs

12:07.950 --> 12:09.950
Chop Suey

12:07.950 --> 12:09.950
7 Points

12:07.950 --> 12:09.950
4 Points

12:07.950 --> 12:09.950
10 Points

12:10.200 --> 12:11.200
Ten points?

12:11.200 --> 12:13.830
By the way, today's breakfast was four points.

12:13.830 --> 12:16.040
Yesterday's dinner was seven points.

12:16.040 --> 12:18.210
Is that a point system?

12:18.210 --> 12:25.720
Crab Cream Croquette

12:18.210 --> 12:25.720
Carbonara

12:18.210 --> 12:25.720
Tom Yum Goong

12:18.210 --> 12:25.720
6 Points

12:18.210 --> 12:25.720
7 Points

12:18.210 --> 12:25.720
3 Points

12:18.540 --> 12:22.510
Since the number of meals is big, and it's tough to evaluate them,

12:22.510 --> 12:25.720
I just use a simple point system.

12:25.720 --> 12:28.890
Isn't that scary for the person who made the food?

12:29.390 --> 12:30.890
Can you cook?

12:31.270 --> 12:36.230
I can, but the finished product should not be eaten.

12:37.020 --> 12:40.900
It seems my family and cooking don't get along.

12:41.230 --> 12:43.740
In other words, you can't.

12:46.030 --> 12:47.530
So, let's begin.

12:48.450 --> 12:49.530
Please take this.

12:50.660 --> 12:53.000
This book has my ideas for the novel.

12:53.000 --> 12:55.620
Please read it after I go home.

12:56.370 --> 13:01.340
I don't like someone reading what I wrote in front of me.

13:01.340 --> 13:04.470
I see. I'm borrowing this then.

13:04.470 --> 13:07.340
So, what kind of things are hard for you?

13:07.720 --> 13:09.140
Hard for me?

13:09.140 --> 13:11.810
Yeah. Things you can't do.

13:11.810 --> 13:15.850
I think it'll be a good idea for me to remember, so I can confirm it.

13:15.850 --> 13:17.480
It's like being an editor.

13:17.770 --> 13:19.400
I see.

13:19.400 --> 13:25.110
The obstacle is that I can't finish writing in one day.

13:25.110 --> 13:26.490
Time is the problem after all.

13:26.780 --> 13:29.990
I forget memories and details.

13:30.570 --> 13:36.040
The story, setting, and even my impression of the characters change.

13:36.040 --> 13:41.340
Many times, I've failed halfway through writing and ended up redoing the story.

13:41.340 --> 13:46.340
By the way, it seems I tried 31 times in four years.

13:46.340 --> 13:51.850
31 times, eh? It'll be my job to challenge that number, then.

13:51.850 --> 13:55.350
I don't know. I'll leave it to you.

13:55.350 --> 13:58.850
Roger. Is there anything else I should pay attention to?

13:58.850 --> 13:59.730
Erm...

13:59.730 --> 14:00.230
Hm?

14:00.230 --> 14:01.060
Ah, nothing.

14:01.310 --> 14:05.320
What's wrong? Tell me everything that's on your mind now.

14:05.320 --> 14:09.820
Erm, there was a question in my math class.

14:10.360 --> 14:13.280
A stake is driven in a field, and a sheep is tied to it.

14:14.240 --> 14:16.620
The sheep keeps munching the grass.

14:16.620 --> 14:19.290
What is the area of the resulting circle?

14:19.670 --> 14:23.340
The square of the length of the string times pi, right?

14:23.340 --> 14:26.800
It seems the sheep even eats the roots of the grass.

14:27.590 --> 14:31.800
The grass can't grow back, and the plain turns into a desert.

14:31.800 --> 14:39.480
When I heard this question, I saw an image of that tied sheep slowly starving to death.

14:40.810 --> 14:43.310
For this novel, I...

14:45.730 --> 14:47.690
Nah, it's nothing.

14:48.610 --> 14:52.110
I misunderstood. It's nothing.

14:52.110 --> 14:53.320
But...

14:53.320 --> 14:54.990
Please forget what I said just now.

14:55.280 --> 14:59.370
R-Really? I won't write it down in my diary then.

14:59.620 --> 15:02.210
You keep a diary too?

15:02.210 --> 15:03.710
Nah, not at all.

15:03.960 --> 15:05.090
Geez.

15:11.010 --> 15:14.300
You're showing your honesty in the wrong place.

15:14.300 --> 15:17.890
Even if you didn't say it... but...

15:30.030 --> 15:31.450
What are you doing?

15:31.450 --> 15:34.070
I'm sketching. It's practice for drawing.

15:35.490 --> 15:37.490
Can you draw manga?

15:37.490 --> 15:41.790
Manga, eh. You can't draw a manga if you don't have a story.

15:41.790 --> 15:46.130
Story? Should I try to think of one?

15:46.130 --> 15:47.210
You?

15:47.210 --> 15:50.130
Yeah. I like to do that.

15:50.970 --> 15:51.630
Okay.

15:53.630 --> 15:57.890
Onii-chan, I just bought this month's issue. Let's read it together.

15:53.630 --> 15:58.640
The manga she's holding is called Good Pals.

15:58.640 --> 16:02.140
The protagonist will definitely... and then...

16:05.860 --> 16:10.190
Hey, Onii-chan. Shiori or Shimiko, which one do you like?

16:10.190 --> 16:11.860
Hmm, let's see...

16:11.860 --> 16:13.400
This is hard.

16:14.360 --> 16:15.870
Let me take a look.

16:15.870 --> 16:19.620
Ah, please don't read it yet. It's embarrassing.

16:19.620 --> 16:21.450
Eh, what's wrong about that? Show me.

16:20.290 --> 16:21.450
No.

16:23.160 --> 16:25.250
Onii-chan, let's go to the beach.

16:25.250 --> 16:29.170
But I made a promise to Chihiro that we would draw manga together.

16:29.380 --> 16:33.670
Chihiro has something to do today, so... please?

16:35.510 --> 16:38.720
Onee-chan. Onii-chan.

16:38.720 --> 16:40.220
WE'RE GOING TO
THE BEACH

17:07.250 --> 17:09.170
It's all my fault.

17:10.710 --> 17:12.340
Kei...

17:15.550 --> 17:18.800
Because I... stole a march on her.

17:19.600 --> 17:22.810
I don't have the right to tell him my feelings.

17:22.810 --> 17:25.560
Are you making excuses for yourself?

17:26.600 --> 17:31.270
You have always been treading the same ground.

17:32.070 --> 17:37.780
You want someone to grab your hand and take you somewhere one day.

17:41.910 --> 17:43.040
Hello.

17:43.040 --> 17:46.160
Ah, is this Kei? I need to talk to you about something.

17:46.960 --> 17:49.580
It's not something we can discuss on the phone. Can we meet?

17:49.580 --> 17:51.590
Yeah, that's fine.

17:56.050 --> 17:57.800
Excuse me for disturbing you.

17:57.800 --> 17:59.840
Come over and play again anytime.

17:59.840 --> 18:02.050
Yes. Thank you very much.

18:02.050 --> 18:03.930
Chihiro, see you tomorrow.

18:04.220 --> 18:05.680
Yes, see you tomorrow.

18:07.850 --> 18:08.640
Excuse me...

18:08.640 --> 18:09.650
What is it?

18:09.650 --> 18:13.570
Have we met before?

18:13.570 --> 18:15.070
Many times.

18:15.070 --> 18:17.320
Since I'm Himura's friend.

18:17.320 --> 18:19.910
So I know everything about you.

18:19.910 --> 18:23.030
As I thought. I'm sorry.

18:23.030 --> 18:24.870
Nah, don't worry about it.

18:25.450 --> 18:27.870
Oh yeah. I'll teach you a song.

18:27.870 --> 18:28.870
A song?

18:29.620 --> 18:37.090
Iku yamakawa koesari yukaba sabishisa no, hatenamu kuni zo kyou mo tabi yuku.

18:37.720 --> 18:39.800
It's written by Wakayama Bokusui.

18:40.090 --> 18:41.470
What does it mean?

18:42.140 --> 18:47.930
"How many mountains and rivers must I cross to reach the country where there's no loneliness?"

18:47.930 --> 18:53.980
"Even though I know no such country actually exists, I too set out on a new journey today."

18:54.270 --> 18:58.440
It's a cheerful song, even though it mentions loneliness.

18:58.440 --> 19:00.820
I learned this song from Himura.

19:01.780 --> 19:05.830
I bet he learned it by heart a long time ago for someone's sake.

19:09.910 --> 19:10.830
Welcome back.

19:10.830 --> 19:12.290
I'm back.

19:12.830 --> 19:13.830
Did you have fun?

19:13.830 --> 19:14.880
Yes.

19:14.880 --> 19:16.960
Really? I'm glad to hear it.

19:20.420 --> 19:21.970
Oh, sorry I asked you over so late.

19:22.300 --> 19:24.600
Hmm, did someone come over?

19:24.600 --> 19:27.260
Hmm, yeah. Anyway, come in.

19:29.680 --> 19:31.100
Yo. Good evening.

19:31.100 --> 19:32.600
Ah, you're the one this morning...

19:32.600 --> 19:35.270
Tsutsumi Kyosuke. You know him, right?

19:35.270 --> 19:38.150
He's in the same class as me, and he's a member of the film research club.

19:38.150 --> 19:41.280
Now I'm an ex-member of the film research club.

19:41.280 --> 19:43.910
He's got something to discuss with you.

19:43.910 --> 19:44.620
With me?

19:44.870 --> 19:46.870
Yeah. Actually...

19:47.330 --> 19:48.870
I want you to go out with me.

19:48.870 --> 19:50.040
Heh?!

19:53.460 --> 19:55.960
"The girl is the only one in the world."

19:55.960 --> 19:58.460
"The girl is the only one in the world."

19:58.460 --> 20:00.460
"That made her the god of this world."

20:01.260 --> 20:04.470
"She found herself on an island when she began to understand things around her."

20:05.340 --> 20:09.770
"The island was small, and one could go around it in half a day by foot."

20:09.770 --> 20:13.270
"All she could see at the beach was the ocean, the sky,

20:13.270 --> 20:17.480
clouds and the horizon stretching as far as she could see in a 360-degree view."

20:17.770 --> 20:19.480
"There was a mansion on the island."

20:20.070 --> 20:25.160
"There were a huge amount of preserved foods and daily necessities inside the warehouse of the castle,

20:25.160 --> 20:27.490
so she did not have to starve."

20:27.490 --> 20:31.500
"There were tons of books which she couldn't finish reading, even if she spent her whole life."

20:32.000 --> 20:34.000
"They contained everything in this world."

20:35.370 --> 20:40.050
"The stories written in the books were all about people."

20:40.630 --> 20:43.130
"People cannot live alone."

20:43.130 --> 20:46.260
"There were many books with that written in them."

20:46.930 --> 20:49.350
"However, the girl was alone."

20:49.350 --> 20:51.470
"She lived by herself."

20:51.470 --> 20:57.770
"Laughing, crying, things that were previously of value, none of them were needed."

20:59.610 --> 21:04.570
"They were finished. They were completed."

21:05.860 --> 21:11.030
"The girl was the first 'average' person in human history."

21:12.120 --> 21:17.670
"The average of the statistics is exactly the same as the sum of herself."

21:20.590 --> 21:23.300
"That's why everything she does is correct."

21:23.710 --> 21:27.630
"And at the same time, everything could be wrong."

21:33.180 --> 21:34.600
Sheep...

21:38.310 --> 21:44.110
The area of the circle is the square of the length of the chain times 3.14.

21:44.360 --> 21:46.490
The length of the chain is twelve years.

21:46.490 --> 21:49.950
It has always been the same length since the accident four years ago.

21:49.950 --> 21:53.410
The stretchable length of the arm is thirteen hours.

21:53.410 --> 21:56.870
That's everything of me right now.

22:09.430 --> 22:16.770
yumemiteta hitori

22:09.430 --> 22:16.770
I dreamed of being alone

22:17.980 --> 22:28.280
sora miage itsuka mabushii ta

22:17.980 --> 22:28.280
Looking up at the sky which once had dazzled me

22:28.530 --> 22:37.000
itami wo omoidasu no

22:28.530 --> 22:37.000
I remember my pain

22:37.080 --> 22:48.550
shiroi hane ni kaze wo fuke

22:37.080 --> 22:48.550
Blow wind, to the white feathers

22:48.880 --> 23:00.270
yureru kioku ni kagi wo toke

22:48.880 --> 23:00.270
Unlock the key to my wavering memories

23:00.350 --> 23:11.530
todoke hate made douka kanata he

23:00.350 --> 23:11.530
Please reach the other side, even if it means the very end

23:11.910 --> 23:20.410
egao anata ni modoru

23:11.910 --> 23:20.410
I will return the smile to your face

23:20.710 --> 23:23.290
ashita he

23:20.710 --> 23:23.290
Towards tomorrow

23:28.090 --> 23:32.300
Both anxiety and fear will be washed away by the rain of time.

23:32.760 --> 23:36.430
Next episode, ef - a tale of memories:

23:36.430 --> 23:37.350
Rain.

23:37.970 --> 23:40.770
Do you have memories you don't want to forget?
